  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stakeholder meeting on Sustainable (nature based) solutions for the Eastern Ghanaian Coast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To share first ideas on Nature-based coastal protection, the responsible Ghanaian governmental organisations will organise a broad stakeholder meeting in June 2024 in Ghana. This meeting will serve as a platform to engage with these stakeholders, align on the project goals and objectives, establish clear roles and responsibilities, set timelines and milestones, create detailed roadmaps for implementation, and agree on communication and decision-making processes. The outcome of this meeting should be a shared understanding of the project scope, a commitment to collaborative efforts, a unified vision for achieving the desired goals, and a roadmap outlining the steps to be taken to ensure successful project delivery. Additionally, clear action plans, monitoring mechanisms, and evaluation criteria should be defined to measure progress and address any challenges that may arise throughout the project implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
